id: pm-s1fw0x
title: Bind enum recovery examples to the refused operand before rewriting argv
description: "The generic enum guidance fallback uses the first provided value flag to build an example from message prose. With argv --pm-path /selected context --depth invalid, provided flags --pm-path and --depth, and message Value must be one of brief|full, the displayed example becomes pm --pm-path brief context --depth invalid. Bind substitutions to a verified refused flag or omit the speculative retry. PR #1696 now withholds prose-derived choices/retries whenever a producer domain is supplied; the no-domain legacy branch needs its own operand provenance fix."
type: Issue
status: open
priority: 2
tags[4]: context,recovery,sdk,ux
created_at: "2026-11-09T17:08:57.119Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-09T17:20:57.408Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 45
acceptance_criteria: An enum example rewrites only a verified refused value operand while preserving tracker selectors and all unrelated arguments; A missing or ambiguous refused-operand binding withholds a speculative retry and keeps usable contract inspection guidance; A regression reproduces the first-global-flag corruption before repair and verifies an executable scoped retry or explicit withheld-retry result afterward
parent: pm-f05lsg
risk: medium
confidence: high
expected_result: "An enum example changes only the verified refused operand, preserves tracker and extension selectors, and is withheld when the operand cannot be bound safely."
actual_result: "Direct formatter control without a declared recovery domain rewrites --pm-path to brief instead of changing --depth, using the first provided value flag. The declared-domain counterpart is covered by the active PR repair."
